DESCRIPTION:In early modern Venice\, sex workers were frequently accused o
 f practicing magic and witchcraft\, subsequently facing trial before the H
 oly Office. Drawing upon this empirical evidence\, this project examines h
 undreds of Inquisition files spanning the years 1580 to 1630 to reconstruc
 t these women's social networks. The objective is to contextualize and int
 erpret the complex interrelationships between magic\, sex work\, and gende
 r dynamics in early modern society. Adopting a microhistorical approach t
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://cesta.stanford.edu\nLast synced: 2026-
