DESCRIPTION:Description: \n\nBook Talk with Amanda Smith\n\n"Hydrofeminism
  posits that water is a life-giving body that permeates other bodies and b
 lurs corporeal boundaries. According to this theory\, water is thus a subj
 ect from which and with which to think. Building on this premise\, I sugge
 st that if we are always thinking with water (Chen\, MacLeod\, Neimanis)\,
  then creative processes necessarily rely on aqueous ecologies while also 
 interacting with and making them. Based on my forthcoming book\, The Natur
 e of\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Building 260\, Pigott Hall
