BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Hamid and Christina Moghadam Program in Iranian Studies] Witness 
 to Iran’s Paradigm Shift: From Flight PS752 to Woman\, Life\, Freedom an
 d Beyond
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261029T200000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53745897362219-53745897362220@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In this lecture\, Babak Payami argues that the Woman\, Life\, 
 Freedom uprising was not simply another episode in Iran’s long struggle 
 for freedom. It marked the collapse of a political dialogue with power sus
 tained for decades by repression\, ideological rivalry\, and the recurring
  illusion of reform. A generation born after Ayatollah Khomeini’s death 
 has moved beyond seeking concessions within the Islamic Republic’s frame
 work. Its struggle is increasingly directed at the framework itself\, repl
 acing\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:In person at Stanford
END:VEVENT
