 26-11-09T12:50:00-08:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:NEPA and its California counterpart\, CEQA\, require the gover
 nment to study a project’s environmental effects and hear from the publi
 c before building or approving it. Proponents argue those reviews give com
 munities a voice and expose potential harms. Critics point to those same p
 rocess being used to delay green energy\, transmission lines\, and apartme
 nts near transit. \nProposed reforms have ignited a fierce debate. The Se
 nate’s Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act (BAAJA) would cap
  the\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/is-environm
 ental-review-worth-the-wait/\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
